Fixed eight integer fields (`DNSZone.ttl`, `soa_refresh`, `soa_retry`, `soa_expire`, `soa_serial`, `soa_minimum`, `DNSRecord._ttl`, and the abstract `DNSModel.ttl`) that had an artificially high floor (`MinValueValidator(300)`) blocking valid sub-300-second values, and an incorrect ceiling (signed 32-bit maximum). All fields now enforce the unsigned 32-bit range (`0..4294967295`) per RFC 8767 §4 (TTL) and RFC 1035 §3.3.13 (SOA fields, with RFC 1982 §7 governing SERIAL's uint32 range and arithmetic). Also fixed a pre-existing bug where a record-level TTL of `0` was treated as unset and silently replaced by the zone TTL.
